  "name": "Break down a reference video: shot list, contact sheets, report",
  "description": "Pick a video from the asset library. Code first measures every cut and each shot's motion (free, not guessed by a model) and grabs two frames per shot into contact sheets; optionally transcribe the speech so lines are assigned to each shot by timecode. A vision model then judges framing, camera work, transitions and rhythm shot by shot, and writes a picture description plus a storyboard prompt to recreate it (up to 25 shots per call; code reconciles afterwards: out-of-vocabulary words are dropped, and camera moves the pixels don't show are corrected and recorded). Code produces the shot-list report, a model writes the breakdown (structure, pacing curve, hook, reusable techniques), and it is saved as a note and handed over. Cost: no extra spend per shot, 25 shots per vision call — a one-minute, 30-shot video costs two vision calls plus one chat call for the summary. The starting point is a video already in the asset library; to break down a link, import it into the library first with Import from link.",
  "graph_hash": "5993f8d7d70d14cb2f7092dbf71d8fc07d8493c78f84aa63120677e5fe902863",
